    {
      "layer": "economic_commercial",
      "tag": "trade_route_control",
      "direction": "rise",
      "description": "Swabia's position at the headwaters of both the Rhine and upper Danube gave it access to multiple trade routes. The imperial free cities (Augsburg, Ulm, Constance) that developed in Swabia became commercial centers generating revenues that outlasted ducal governance.",
